-- title:
--   Quadratic twist lowering the q-exponent of a newform
-- statement:
--   Let $M$ be a nonzero natural number and let $g$ be a weight-two cusp form on $\Gamma_0(M)$ which is a newform, i.e. a normalised eigenform (multiplicative $q$-coefficients with $a_1=1$ and the usual recursions at prime powers) whose eigensystem away from $M$ is not matched by a normalised eigenform of proper level dividing $M$. Let $S$ be a finite set of primes and $\chi_g$ a ring homomorphism from the Hecke algebra $\mathrm{heckeAlgebra}\ M\ 2\ S$ (the $\mathbb{Z}$-algebra generated by the operators $T_\ell$, $\ell\nmid M$, and $U_r$, $r\mid M$, outside $S$) to $\mathbb{C}$ sending $T_\ell$ to $a_\ell(g)$ for every prime $\ell\nmid M$ with $\ell\notin S$; let $K$ be a field of characteristic zero and $\varphi$ a ring homomorphism from the range of $\chi_g$ to $K$. Let $q$ be a prime with $q^2\mid M$. Assume given a nonzero function $\Phi$ on the adelic group $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_\mathbb{Q})$ which is an adelic lift of $g$ (left invariant under the global points $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Q})$, right invariant under the level-one subgroup at level $M$, and agreeing with the weight-two slash action of the archimedean component of $g$ at $i$ on elements with trivial finite component and positive archimedean determinant), characters $\mu_1,\mu_2:\mathbb{Q}_q^\times\to\mathbb{C}^\times$, and a nonzero $\mathbb{C}$-linear map $f$ from the span $\mathrm{AdelicSpan}\ \Phi$ to the principal series carrier $\mathrm{PSCarrier}\ q\ \mu_1\ \mu_2$ which is $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Q}_q)$-equivariant, with $\mu_1^{-1}\mu_2$ unramified (trivial on all $u\in\mathbb{Q}_q^\times$ with $\|u\|=1$). Then there exist a nonzero modulus $m$ with either $q$ odd and $m=q$, or $q=2$ and $m=8$; a character $\chi:(\mathbb{Z}/m)^\times\to K^\times$ with $\chi(u)^2=1$ for all $u$ and $\chi\neq 1$; a nonzero level $M'$ with $q^2\nmid M'$; a weight-two newform $h$ on $\Gamma_0(M')$; a finite set of primes $S'$ and a ring homomorphism $\chi_h$ from $\mathrm{heckeAlgebra}\ M'\ 2\ S'$ to $\mathbb{C}$ with $\chi_h(T_\ell)=a_\ell(h)$ for all primes $\ell\nmid M'$ outside $S'$; and a ring homomorphism $\varphi'$ from the range of $\chi_h$ to $K$, such that for every prime $\ell$ with $\ell\nmid M$, $\ell\nmid M'$, $\ell\notin S$, $\ell\notin S'$ and $\ell$ coprime to $m$ one has $\varphi(\chi_g(T_\ell))=\chi(\ell\bmod m)\,\varphi'(\chi_h(T_\ell))$.
--
--   This is the twisting step of Atkin–Li theory in the form needed on the level-lowering route: if the local component of the newform $g$ at $q$ maps equivariantly and nontrivially to a principal series whose ratio of inducing characters is unramified, then $g$ becomes, after twisting by a quadratic Dirichlet character of conductor a power of $q$, a newform of level with $q$-exponent at most one, the comparison of Hecke eigenvalues being recorded through the chosen embeddings of the eigenvalue rings into $K$. It is used in the analysis of the characteristic polynomial of inertia at $q$ for the associated Galois representation.
